# 0006. Secrets never in the repo: untracked secrets file, global gitleaks hook

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

Credentials live only in an untracked, mode-600 file, and every commit on the machine, in
any repo, is scanned for secrets first.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: the old `.zshrc` held API keys (an OpenAI key committed in `fc48ec7` had to be
  revoked on 2026-11-07). A public dotfiles repo must not leak credentials, here or in any
  other repo.
- **Local files**: `conf.d/90-local.zsh` sources `~/.config/zsh/local.zsh` (machine-only
  settings, see `local.zsh.example`) and `~/.config/zsh/secrets.zsh` last.
- **Adding a secret**: `secret-add NAME` (UPPER_CASE only) reads the value without echo,
  writes `export NAME=...` to the secrets file (created `chmod 600`, old line replaced) and
  exports it; never in history or the repo.
- **Migration**: `scripts/migrate-secrets.sh OLD_ZSHRC` (`make secrets FILE=...`, and
  automatically from `link.sh` when it backs up an old `~/.zshrc`) moves `export` lines whose
  name contains `KEY`, `TOKEN`, `SECRET`, `PASSWORD`, `PASSWD` or `CREDENTIAL(S)` into the
  secrets file, printing names only.
- **Global hook**: `git/config` sets `core.hooksPath = ~/.config/git/hooks` (linked from
  `git/hooks`). Every hook name there is a symlink to `git/hooks/_dispatch`, which:
  - at `pre-commit`, runs `gitleaks git --pre-commit --staged --redact` and stops the commit
    on a finding, with hints (`gitleaks:allow` comment for a false positive);
  - warns, without blocking, when gitleaks isn't installed;
  - then `exec`s the repo's own `.git/hooks/<name>` if executable, so per-repo hooks still
    run.
- **Known findings**: `.gitleaksignore` holds one fingerprint per line with the reason
  (the revoked OpenAI key). `leaks` scans a repo's history and tree on demand.
- **Rule**: no `--no-verify` or `SKIP_GITLEAKS=1` for routine work.
- **Consequences**: every repo on the machine is scanned without setup. Repos using the
  pre-commit framework need `git config --local core.hooksPath .git/hooks` (gotcha 6).

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: gitleaks, git `core.hooksPath`, POSIX sh.
- Alternatives: per-repo pre-commit framework: easy to forget in a new repo; a password
  manager CLI at startup: a process and maybe network per shell.
